M2.3: PS/2 keyboard - first real input path

- kbd.c: IRQ1, ports 0x60/0x64, scancode set 1 -> ASCII table
  (letters/digits/punct/enter/tab/esc/backspace/space), both shift
  keys tracked through make+break, E0/E1 prefix follow-up escaping,
  power-of-two ring buffer (2^7) so the IRQ never blocks, break codes
  never reach the consumer. Controller stat bit 0 gates every read.
- main.c: block-on-hlt key consumer echoing each key to VGA + serial,
  10 events as the milestone gate.

QEMU evidence: 'sendkey h e l l o spc k e r n' through the monitor
produces "hello kern" then "kbd: 10 events consumed" on serial -
end-to-end interrupt->driver->decode->buffer->consumer->consoles.

Note: table comments verified against the classic IBM set-1 map row
by row (0x1D ctrl, 0x2A lshift, 0x36 rshift, 0x39 space); mouse
packets (shared controller, IRQ12) deliberately untouched in M2.3.
